@startuml 02-architecture
title X3 Thermal Printer - components and interfaces
skinparam componentStyle uml2

package "PC (Linux)" {
  component "x3gui.sh" as SH <<start wrapper>>
  component "x3gui.py" as GUI <<GTK3 user interface>>
  component "i18n.py" as I18N <<translations>>
  component "x3print.py" as CORE <<rendering + protocol>>
  component "assets/" as ASSETS <<icon, example image>>

  package "CUPS integration" {
    component "cups/x3bridge.py" as BRIDGE <<bridge, no sudo>>
    component "cups/x3raster.py" as RASTER <<filter, variant B>>
    component "cups/x3bt.py" as BACKEND <<backend, variant B>>
  }
  component "CUPS" as CUPS <<queue X3Thermo>>
  component "BlueZ / RFCOMM" as BLUEZ <<Bluetooth stack>>
  database "~/.config/x3drucker.json" as CFG
}

cloud "thermal paper" {
  component "X3 print head" as HEAD <<864 dots @ 300 dpi>>
}

SH --> GUI : starts
GUI --> CORE : render_*()
GUI --> I18N : t()
GUI --> ASSETS : icon, start image
GUI --> CFG : settings
CORE --> BLUEZ : RFCOMM channel 1
BLUEZ --> HEAD : YK/YZW frames

CUPS --> BRIDGE : socket://127.0.0.1:9101
BRIDGE --> CORE : uses the renderers
BRIDGE --> BLUEZ
CUPS --> RASTER : PDF/PS (variant B)
RASTER --> BACKEND : frames
BACKEND --> BLUEZ

note right of CORE
  YK/YZW frame:
  64 cmd seq len_lo len_hi
  payload ... 00 00 00 00 9b
end note
@enduml
